  mortgage_tp_fixed_rate_what: 'A fixed rate stays the same for an agreed time. Your monthly payment does not change during that time, whatever happens in the market. Often the rate is fixed only for the first few years and then becomes variable.',
  mortgage_tp_fixed_rate_why: 'You know exactly what you will pay, so planning your budget is easy. The price for that calm is that a fixed rate is often a little higher at the start than a variable one.',
  mortgage_tp_fixed_rate_how: 'There is no extra formula. The bank calculates the payment from the fixed rate, the loan amount and the term, and that payment stays until the fixed period ends.',
